    "narrative": "The core of our lineup today revolves around high-upside matchups against favorable arms, with **Corbin Carroll** leading the way at an elite 85.94 score. Facing Paredes, **Corbin Carroll** benefits from a massive 19% SP skill boost and optimal top-of-the-order placement, making him our highest-projected source of counting stats. **Gabriel Moreno** and **Brice Turang** also offer elite floor-to-ceiling potential; **Brice Turang** is particularly intriguing given the 4.25 xERA of the opposing starter and a +4% bump attributed to a slow delivery that essentially guarantees a green light on the basepaths. Meanwhile, **James Wood** remains a must-start at 65.62, leveraging an elite .404 xwOBA and top-order duties to mitigate the park disadvantage against Martinez.\n\nWe are navigating a few tricky marginal calls, specifically with our infield depth. The most difficult bench decision involved **Max Muncy**, who carried a 45.66 score but was ultimately squeezed out by the efficiency of our middle-infield options. While **Max Muncy** enjoys a nice park factor, his 9th-order spot created a drag on his value compared to the platoon-advantaged **Travis Bazzana**. We are also keeping a close watch on **Tyler Soderstrom**, whose 46.34 score is buoyed by park factors but anchored by a brutal matchup against the 3.23 xERA of Detmers. **Kyle Karros** faces similar headwinds, dropping to a 47.89 score due to an elite catcher matchup and a suboptimal 8th-order slot.\n\nRisk mitigation is central to today\u2019s strategy, especially regarding our SB-heavy profile. We are proceeding with **Jose Caballero** despite a shaky 42.92 projection; his score is suppressed by a severe platoon disadvantage against Burns, yet his ability to swipe bags makes him a necessary evil in our pursuit of category scarcity. We continue to monitor the status of **Mickey Moniak** and **Trevor Story**, who remain sidelined on the IL, leaving our bench depth slightly thinned. With **Alex Freeland** and **Zach McKinstry** holding down the lower end of the daily efficiency spectrum, we are leaning heavily on the top-tier production of **Corbin Carroll**, **James Wood**, and **Austin Riley** to carry our 5x5 prospects across the finish line.",
